  "verbalization": "Osugacestat is implicated in the biological pathway leading to HaCaT cell activation through multiple indirect mechanisms. The evidence suggests that Osugacestat targets UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2A1, which is subsequently targeted by Acetoxyisovalerylalkannin and Neranic acid. These compounds, in turn, have a target of HaCaT, indicating a chain of molecular interactions that ultimately result in cellular effects on HaCaT cells. The presence of multiple targets in the pathway highlights the complexity of the relationship, with Osugacestat acting as a central node in a network of interactions that ultimately influence HaCaT. The integration of these pathways suggests that Osugacestat may exert its effects through a series of enzymatic and cellular processes that are not fully elucidated, but which collectively contribute to the observed interaction with HaCaT.",
